---
/**
 * Which reproduction of the drawing package you are reading.
 *
 * The two themes are not "light" and "dark" on this site — they are the two
 * ways a drawing gets reproduced. One is printed on paper, one is run as a
 * blueprint, and the tokens are already named for it. The control says that
 * rather than naming a brightness.
 *
 * The buttons are in the markup but the sheet keeps them hidden until the
 * inline script in the head confirms scripting and adds `has-theme-control`.
 * That is the rule the drawing zoom already follows: a control that cannot
 * work should not be drawn. Rendering them hidden rather than injecting them
 * later is what keeps the head band from shifting once the script runs.
 *
 * Nothing here decides the initial theme. The head script does that before
 * first paint, so a pinned sheet never flashes the other reproduction first.
 */
---

<div class="themeswitch" role="group" aria-label="Reproduction">
  <button class="themeswitch__opt" type="button" data-theme-set="light" aria-pressed="false">
    Paper
  </button>
  <button class="themeswitch__opt" type="button" data-theme-set="dark" aria-pressed="false">
    Blueprint
  </button>
</div>

<script>
  import '../scripts/theme';
</script>
